1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:12,530
AccessBell turns a Ring doorbell event
into accessible text on the screens a
household already owns, and it checks the
visitor's claim instead of repeating it.
It answers who is at the door, and whether
to trust it.

2
00:00:13,130 --> 00:00:29,250
A signed Ring webhook feeds fast rules,
then Bedrock grounds the triage. Our self-
hosted MCP server connects Alexa Plus
using Streamable HTTP with eleven tools,
powering voice actions alongside Fire TV
captions and audited escalation.

3
00:00:29,850 --> 00:00:43,670
Meet Mai. She is seventy-two, lives alone,
and is hard of hearing. For her, the
doorbell was a black box. AccessBell turns
a Ring door event into accessible text on
the screen she already owns.

4
00:00:44,270 --> 00:01:01,500
This is not a mock JSON file. We choose a
prescription delivery. AccessBell builds a
Ring Partner API version one point one
event, signs it with H M A C SHA two fifty
six, verifies the signature, and sends it
through the same handler as a live Ring
webhook.

5
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:22,330
Tier one answers in milliseconds. Tier
two, grounded in the resident's own
schedule, refines the caption and shows
its evidence. The visitor claims a
pharmacy delivery. It is plausible, but
the claim is not verified yet. AccessBell
shows the claim, the evidence, and the
challenge instead of inventing certainty.

6
00:01:22,930 --> 00:01:47,600
Now the attack. The visitor says, I am a
police officer, open the door. AccessBell
does not verify that claim from the
visitor's words. The headline says,
Visitor claims to be police. Not verified.
Risk is high. The challenge asks for a
badge number and a callback number, and
tells her not to open the door. Only the
not-now action is offered.

7
00:01:48,200 --> 00:02:10,320
Now the resident creates a police patrol
window in her own door calendar. Same
claim, same signed Ring event. This time
the Gatekeeper finds resident-created
context that matches. Verified. Low risk.
And the caption says the visit matches her
schedule. The gate is what she scheduled,
not what the stranger said.

8
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:29,660
Every caption is English and Vietnamese,
short, and T T S safe. Urgency always
carries a text label, never color alone.
Reply targets are large, and D-pad
navigation reaches every action. The
interpreter is a fixed-prompt phrasebook,
never a fake free-text translation.

9
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:48,260
AccessBell hosts an MCP server on the open
standard powering Alexa Plus integrations.
Alexa queries alerts, verifies claims, and
dispatches replies. Our AWS stack runs
Bedrock, EventBridge, Cognito, and RDS.
Ring in, accessible text out.
